   "description": "Strong positive interaction with sign reversals. Increasing l5 from 0 to 10 changes average log-odds by -0.49 when l8=0, but +2.53 when l8=10. Increasing l8 from 0 to 10 changes average log-odds by -0.81 when l5=0, but +2.21 when l5=10.",
   "where": "Smooth transitions: the average l5 endpoint contrast crosses zero near l8=1.5; the average l8 endpoint contrast crosses zero near l5=2.6."
  },
  {
   "inputs": [
    "l7",
    "l8"
   ],
   "description": "Increasing l7 from 0 to 10 raises average log-odds by about 0.43 at l8=0, but lowers it by about 0.45 at l8=10.",
   "where": "The average l7 endpoint contrast reverses near l8=3.7."
  },
  {
   "inputs": [
    "age_c",
    "l10"
   ],
   "description": "Higher l10 attenuates the age effect. The average age-18-to-90 log-odds increase falls from about 3.40 at l10=0 to 2.62 at l10=10.",
   "where": "Gradual attenuation across l10=0–10 and age_c=-4.2–3."
  },
  {
   "inputs": [
    "wfns45",
    "surgery",
    "l5"
   ],
   "description": "Both the positive WFNS contrast and the magnitude of the negative treatment contrast peak at intermediate l5, then weaken. At l5=3 versus 10, these contrasts are approximately +1.86 versus +1.50, and -1.74 versus -1.43 log-odds.",
